* The coarse path is the only thing that filters when a page is very small.
  Below one eighth scale the atlas runs out of mip levels -- the gutter around
  each glyph is what bounds the chain -- so the detailed path starts aliasing
  again if --coarse-below is lowered past the default. Page backgrounds and the
  caret are untextured quads and alias at every size.
